    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Opioid antagonists (naltrexone, nalmefene) and GABA-receptor modulators (baclofen, acamprosate) appear to give short-term benefit by reducing craving and withdrawal; evidence for disulfiram is not as strong."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Alcohol withdrawal requires benzodiazepines (eg, diazepam); in advanced liver disease, excessive sedation can precipitate portosystemic encephalopathy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A nutritious diet and vitamin supplements (especially B vitamins) are important in the first days of abstinence."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
